# Vite serves this directory verbatim at the site root, so it has to be
# committed. It is re-included explicitly because a `Public/` rule in a global
# ignore file matches it on a case-insensitive filesystem, which silently drops
# every asset in here — the directory has to be re-included, not just the files,
# or git never descends into it.
!public/
